     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S3535\n\nSPONSOR: MAY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization\nof the county of Onondaga to impose an additional rate of sales and\ncompensating use taxes\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend the current authorization for Onondaga County to impose an\nadditional 1% sales tax rate through November 30, 2026.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 -- Authorizes Onondaga County to continue, by local law, the\nadditional 1% sales tax rate through November 30, 2026.\n\nSections 2-4 -- Provides for the distribution of funds raised by the\nadditional rate of tax among units of local government in the County.\n\nSection 5 -- Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation, introduced at the request of Onondaga County, enacts\nan extension of the authorization to impose an additional 1% local sales\ntax rate. This legislation extends such authorization for a local law\nthrough November 30, 2026.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to New York State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
